{
  "$schema": "../../schema/incident.schema.json",
  "protocol": "Cream Finance",
  "name": "Cream Finance yUSD price-per-share collateral inflation",
  "summary": "Cream's PriceOracleProxy priced every registered Yearn-vault collateral as getYvTokenPrice(token) = underlyingPrice * pricePerShare(), reading the vault's live share price with no bound, time-average or sanity check. A bare yCRV transfer into the yUSD vault doubled pricePerShare in the same transaction, so the oracle reported twice the true value for crYUSD collateral and the Comptroller authorised borrows against collateral that did not exist. The contract's own getLPFairPrice and getCrvTokenPrice branches avoid spot quantities for exactly this reason; no value of the only yVault parameters (isYvToken, version) bounds the multiplier, so the defect is in the executed code rather than in a configured value.",
